<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21323] fallocate through a stale fd resets the OST object to the previous owner; quota charged to the old user</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21323</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After a file is chowned, a fallocate from a client that still has the file open with the old owner cached still charges the quota of the old owner, and the new owner is charged nothing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The previous owner is charged for a file they no longer own, and the new owner's usage is not counted against their quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The mismatch stays until the file is chowned again. A chown to the same owner restored the OST object (tested, see below).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;It needs an fd opened before the chown. A fresh open after the chown does not reset the owner (tested, see below).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A plain write and an ftruncate through the same stale fd do not reset the owner (both tested, see below). Only fallocate does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
